IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg3-civil`
IMPORT `bgg3-criminal`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-scope`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-limits`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-courts`
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-appealable`
IMPORT `bgg4-grounds`
IMPORT `bgg4-new-submissions`
IMPORT `bgg4-time-limit`
IMPORT `bgg4-procedure`
IMPORT `bgg4-simplified`
IMPORT `bgg4-cantonal`
IMPORT `bgg4-seams`

-- Federal Supreme Court Act (Bundesgerichtsgesetz, BGG, SR 173.110), chapter 4 (Art. 90 to 112, Beschwerdeverfahren),
-- German consolidated text applicable from 2026-04-01 (a plain-text rendering, not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person affected by a decision (a party to civil or criminal proceedings, or to proceedings in a public-law matter,
-- who lost, or a person with another interest the text names).  The questions are the ones that person asks about the appeal:
-- which decisions may I appeal, on what grounds, by when, what new submissions are allowed, does the appeal stop the decision
-- taking effect, and what must the cantons provide.  There is never a seat for an official: the powers and duties of the
-- Court, the lower instance and the federal authorities appear here only as what they mean for the person.
--
-- This layer restates no rule.  Every question calls a function of layer 1 (bgg4-appealable, bgg4-grounds, bgg4-new-submissions,
-- bgg4-time-limit, bgg4-procedure, bgg4-simplified, bgg4-cantonal, bgg4-seams) with plain inputs, one per fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as the person is asked.  The answer is what the layer-1 function says:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes;   JUST FALSE   the text says no, in its own words;   NOTHING   the text does not decide it.
-- A NOTHING is never a no.  See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".
--
-- Questions that Art 77(2) of chapter 3 reaches (Art 90 to 98, 103(2), 105(2), 106(1), 107(2)) take one more input, whether the
-- appeal is against an arbitral award, and answer NOTHING for such an appeal, because what governs it is outside the text.
--
-- Questions that need only the Act's dates take `Date day month year` as the date input.


§ `Which decisions can I appeal (Art 90 to 94)`

@export May I appeal to the Federal Supreme Court against my decision, because of the kind of decision it is (Art 90 to 93)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the decision ends the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the whole case in the court or authority that made it?
      `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision deal with only some of the claims made in the case?
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can those claims be judged independently of the claims the decision leaves open?
      `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the case for only some of the people who sued or were sued together?
      `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a preliminary or interim step, made before the final decision?
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision sent to you on its own, separately from the final decision?
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision rule on whether the court has jurisdiction, or on a request that a judge step aside?
      `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about international legal assistance in a criminal matter?
      `the matter is in the field of asylum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about asylum?
      `the decision is on extradition detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern detention pending extradition?
      `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern the seizure of assets or valuables?
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the decision cause you harm that could not be put right later?
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would upholding the appeal bring about a final decision straight away?
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that spare a significant amount of time or cost that a long evidence procedure would otherwise take?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 90 0 FALSE
        (`Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against the decision` `the decision ends the proceedings` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others` `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the matter is in the field of asylum` `the decision is on extradition detention` `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`)

@export If my decision is a preliminary or interim decision on jurisdiction or recusal, can I still challenge it later (Art 92(2))?
GIVEN `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a preliminary or interim step, made before the final decision?
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision sent to you on its own, separately from the final decision?
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision rule on whether the court has jurisdiction, or on a request that a judge step aside?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 92(2) my decision on jurisdiction or recusal can be challenged later` IS
    `Art 92(2) the decision can be challenged later` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal`

@export If I could not appeal my other preliminary or interim decision at the time, can I challenge it with the appeal against the final decision (Art 93(3))?
GIVEN `the decision is another preliminary or interlocutory decision, not one on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a preliminary or interim decision other than one on jurisdiction or on a request that a judge step aside?
      `the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2 is not admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal against this decision not allowed at this stage (under Art 92(1) and 93(1) and (2))?
      `no use was made of the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no appeal made against it at this stage although one was allowed?
      `the decision affects the content of the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision affect what the final decision says?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 93(3) my other preliminary decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` IS
    `Art 93(3) the preliminary or interlocutory decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` `the decision is another preliminary or interlocutory decision, not one on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2 is not admissible` `no use was made of the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2` `the decision affects the content of the final decision`

@export May I appeal against an authority's unlawful refusal or delay in deciding (Art 94)?
GIVEN `the authority refused or delayed a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authority refuse to decide, or delay deciding?
      `the refusal or delay is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the refusal or delay unlawful?
      `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision that was refused or delayed one that could be appealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of my decision` IS
    `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` `the authority refused or delayed a decision` `the refusal or delay is unlawful` `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed`


§ `On what grounds (Art 95 to 98)`

@export May I complain to the Federal Supreme Court of a violation of this source of law (Art 95)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the source of law that was violated` IS A `Source of law in Art 95` @desc Which source of law do you say was violated: federal law, international law, cantonal constitutional rights, cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes, intercantonal law, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 95 0 FALSE
        (`Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `the source of law that was violated`)

@export May I complain to the Federal Supreme Court about the application of foreign law (Art 96)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the complaint about foreign law` IS A `Complaint about foreign law` @desc What is the complaint about foreign law: that foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes, that foreign law it makes applicable was applied wrongly, or another complaint?
      `the decision concerns a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern a matter of money or property (a pecuniary matter)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 96 0 FALSE
        (`Art 96 the complaint about foreign law can be raised` `the complaint about foreign law` `the decision concerns a pecuniary matter`)

@export May I complain to the Federal Supreme Court about the lower instance's finding of the facts (Art 97)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance?
      `the finding of the legally relevant facts is wrong or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the finding of the legally relevant facts wrong or incomplete?
      `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the lower instance's finding of the facts obviously wrong?
      `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the finding of the facts rest on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95?
      `correcting the defect can be decisive for the outcome of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could correcting the defect be decisive for the outcome of the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 97 0 FALSE
        (`Art 97 the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` `the finding of the legally relevant facts is wrong or incomplete` `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` `correcting the defect can be decisive for the outcome of the proceedings`)

@export May I raise this complaint against a decision on provisional measures (Art 98)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the appeal is against a decision on provisional measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision on provisional measures?
      `the complaint is of a violation of constitutional rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you complain of a violation of constitutional rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 98 I can raise this complaint against the decision on provisional measures` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 98 0 FALSE
        (`Art 98 the complaint can be raised against the decision on provisional measures` `the appeal is against a decision on provisional measures` `the complaint is of a violation of constitutional rights`)


§ `New submissions (Art 99)`

@export May I put forward a new fact or new evidence before the Federal Supreme Court (Art 99(1))?
GIVEN `the submission is a new fact or new evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you want to put forward a new fact or a new piece of evidence?
      `only the decision of the lower instance gave occasion for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did only the lower instance's decision give occasion for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 99(1) I may put forward the new fact or new evidence` IS
    `Art 99(1) the new fact or new evidence may be put forward` `the submission is a new fact or new evidence` `only the decision of the lower instance gave occasion for it`

@export May I make a new claim before the Federal Supreme Court (Art 99(2))?
GIVEN `the claim is new` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim you want to make new, that is, one not made before the lower instance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 99(2) my new claim is admissible` IS
    `Art 99(2) the new claim is admissible` `the claim is new`


§ `By when must I appeal (Art 100 and 101)`

@export How many days do I have to appeal against a decision (Art 100(1) to (4))?
GIVEN `the kind of decision for the time limit` IS A `Kind of decision in Art 100(2) to (4)` @desc Which kind of decision is it for the time limit: a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy, in international legal assistance in criminal matters or administrative assistance in tax matters, on the return of a child, of the Federal Patent Court on a licence, of a cantonal government on a federal vote, of a cantonal government on a National Council election, or none of these?
      `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Art 100 the number of days I have to appeal against a decision` IS
    `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` `the kind of decision for the time limit` `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement`

@export By what day must I file my appeal (Art 100 and 101)?
GIVEN `what the appeal is brought against` IS A `Act challenged by the appeal` @desc What do you want to appeal against: a decision, a cantonal enactment, or an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision?
      `the kind of decision for the time limit` IS A `Kind of decision in Art 100(2) to (4)` @desc Which kind of decision is it for the time limit: a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy, in international legal assistance in criminal matters or administrative assistance in tax matters, on the return of a child, of the Federal Patent Court on a licence, of a cantonal government on a federal vote, of a cantonal government on a National Council election, or none of these?
      `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement?
      `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the complete version of the decision notified to you?
      `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal about a conflict of competence between two cantons?
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the first canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the second canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` IS A DATE @desc If you appeal against a cantonal enactment: on what day was it published, as cantonal law decides? (Any date otherwise.)
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the rules on suspension or restoration of time limits leave out of the count? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A `Time limit for filing`
DECIDE `Art 100 and 101 the last day on which I can file my appeal` IS
    `Art 100 and 101 the time limit for filing` `what the appeal is brought against` `the kind of decision for the time limit` `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count`

@export Is my appeal in time (Art 100 and 101)?
GIVEN `what the appeal is brought against` IS A `Act challenged by the appeal` @desc What do you want to appeal against: a decision, a cantonal enactment, or an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision?
      `the kind of decision for the time limit` IS A `Kind of decision in Art 100(2) to (4)` @desc Which kind of decision is it for the time limit: a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy, in international legal assistance in criminal matters or administrative assistance in tax matters, on the return of a child, of the Federal Patent Court on a licence, of a cantonal government on a federal vote, of a cantonal government on a National Council election, or none of these?
      `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement?
      `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the complete version of the decision notified to you?
      `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal about a conflict of competence between two cantons?
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the first canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the second canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` IS A DATE @desc If you appeal against a cantonal enactment: on what day was it published, as cantonal law decides? (Any date otherwise.)
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the rules on suspension or restoration of time limits leave out of the count? (0 if none.)
      `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file, or will you file, the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 100 and 101 my appeal is in time` IS
    `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `what the appeal is brought against` `the kind of decision for the time limit` `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court`


§ `Procedure: suspensive effect, provisional measures, the facts and the law (Art 102 to 107)`

@export Will the Court send my appeal to this recipient and set a time limit for observations (Art 102(1))?
GIVEN `service of the appeal on this recipient is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary for the Court to send the appeal to this recipient?
      `the recipient is the lower instance, another party, a participant or an authority entitled to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient the lower instance, another party, another participant, or an authority entitled to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 102(1) the Court must send my appeal to this recipient and set a time limit` IS
    `Art 102(1) the Federal Supreme Court must serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` `service of the appeal on this recipient is necessary` `the recipient is the lower instance, another party, a participant or an authority entitled to appeal`

@export Will there be a further exchange of submissions (Art 102(3))?
GIVEN `the case is an exception to the rule that no further exchange of submissions takes place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case an exception to the rule that there is no further exchange of submissions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 102(3) there will be a further exchange of submissions` IS
    `Art 102(3) a further exchange of submissions takes place` `the case is an exception to the rule that no further exchange of submissions takes place`

@export Does my appeal stop the decision from taking effect (Art 103)? Not for an arbitral award: ask the next question.
GIVEN `what the instructing judge ordered about suspensive effect` IS A `Order on suspensive effect` @desc What did the instructing judge order about suspensive effect: that the appeal has it, that it has none, or nothing?
      `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your civil appeal against a judgment that creates, changes or ends a legal relationship (a formative judgment)?
      `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision impose an unconditional prison sentence or a measure that deprives of liberty?
      `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part of the decision you ask about the decision on civil claims?
      `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings about international legal assistance in a criminal matter?
      `the appeal is against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal against a final order?
      `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal against another order that permits information from the secret sphere to be sent, or objects or assets to be handed over?
      `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings about international administrative assistance in tax matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 103 my appeal stops the decision taking effect` IS
    `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `what the instructing judge ordered about suspensive effect` `the kind of appeal` `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters`

@export Does my appeal stop the decision from taking effect under Art 103(2), if it is an appeal against an arbitral award (Art 103(2) with Art 77(2))?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your civil appeal against a judgment that creates, changes or ends a legal relationship (a formative judgment)?
      `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision impose an unconditional prison sentence or a measure that deprives of liberty?
      `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part of the decision you ask about the decision on civil claims?
      `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings about international legal assistance in a criminal matter?
      `the appeal is against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal against a final order?
      `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal against another order that permits information from the secret sphere to be sent, or objects or assets to be handed over?
      `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings about international administrative assistance in tax matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 103(2) my appeal against an arbitral award stops the decision taking effect` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 103 2 FALSE
        (`Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `the kind of appeal` `the appeal is directed against a formative judgment` `the decision imposes an unconditional custodial sentence or a custodial measure` `the part of the decision concerned is the decision on civil claims` `the proceedings are in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is against a final order` `the appeal is against another order that permits the transmission of information from the secret sphere or the handing over of objects or assets` `the proceedings are in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters`)

@export May the instructing judge order a provisional measure (Art 104)?
GIVEN `the measure is ordered on the judge's own motion or on a party's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure ordered by the judge on their own motion or on a party's request?
      `the measure serves to preserve the existing state of affairs or to secure threatened interests for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the measure preserve the existing state of affairs or secure threatened interests for the time being?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure for me` IS
    `Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure` `the measure is ordered on the judge's own motion or on a party's request` `the measure serves to preserve the existing state of affairs or to secure threatened interests for the time being`

@export Is the Federal Supreme Court bound by the facts the lower instance found (Art 105)? Not for an arbitral award: ask the next question about Art 105(2).
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance?
      `the facts were found by the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these facts ones the lower instance found?
      `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the lower instance's finding of the facts obviously wrong?
      `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the finding of the facts rest on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts the lower instance found` IS
    `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` `the appeal is against a decision on granting or refusing money benefits of the military or accident insurance` `the facts were found by the lower instance` `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95`

@export May the Court correct or supplement the lower instance's finding of the facts, if my appeal is against an arbitral award (Art 105(2) with Art 77(2))?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the lower instance's finding of the facts obviously wrong?
      `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the finding of the facts rest on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 105(2) the Court may correct the finding of the facts in my arbitral appeal` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 105 2 FALSE
        (`Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` `the finding of the facts is obviously wrong` `the finding of the facts rests on a violation of law within the meaning of Art 95`)

@export Will the Federal Supreme Court examine the violation I complain of (Art 106)?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the kind of rule the complaint is about` IS A `Kind of rule in Art 106` @desc Which rule do you say was violated: fundamental rights, cantonal law, intercantonal law, or other law?
      `the complaint was raised in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you raise the complaint in your appeal?
      `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give reasons for the complaint in your appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 106 the Court examines the violation I complain of` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 106 (IF `the kind of rule the complaint is about` EQUALS `other law` THEN 1 ELSE 2) FALSE
        (`Art 106 the Court examines the violation of the rule` `the kind of rule the complaint is about` `the complaint was raised in the appeal` `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal`)

-- Reading the answer: JUST FALSE means no, the Court may not go beyond the claims of the parties.  The text states this without a condition, so no fact is asked (fork F33).
@export May the Court go beyond the claims I made (Art 107(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 107(1) the Court may go beyond my claims` IS
    `Art 107(1) the Court is permitted to go beyond the claims of the parties`

@export If the Court upholds my appeal, may it give this outcome (Art 107(2))?
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an award of an arbitral tribunal (a private arbitration)?
      `the Court upholds the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court uphold the appeal?
      `what the Court does when it upholds the appeal` IS A `Outcome of an upheld appeal` @desc If the Court upholds the appeal, what does it do: decide the matter itself, send it back to the lower instance for a new judgment, send it to the authority that decided as first instance, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds my appeal` IS
    `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` 107 2 (`what the Court does when it upholds the appeal` EQUALS `the Court decides the matter itself`)
        (`Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` `the Court upholds the appeal` `what the Court does when it upholds the appeal`)

@export By what day must the Court decide not to enter on my appeal in international legal assistance or tax assistance (Art 107(3))?
GIVEN `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters?
      `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters?
      `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court consider the appeal inadmissible?
      `an exchange of submissions took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an exchange of submissions take place?
      `the day the exchange of submissions ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the exchange of submissions end? (Any date if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Art 107(3) the last day for the Court to decide not to enter on my appeal` IS
    `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the appeal is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `the Court considers the appeal inadmissible` `an exchange of submissions took place` `the day the exchange of submissions ended`

-- Reading the answer: JUST TRUE means yes, the Court is held to the 15 days for a decision not to enter, because the exception of the second sentence does not apply (fork F34).
-- JUST FALSE means the Court is not held to them (an extradition, the person has no final decision on an asylum application).  NOTHING means the appeal is not in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters.
@export In my extradition appeal, is the Court held to the 15 days for a decision not to enter (Art 107(3), second sentence)?
GIVEN `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters?
      `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 107(3) the Court is held to the 15 days in my extradition appeal` IS
    `Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` `the appeal is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the extradition proceedings concern a person whose asylum application has no final decision with legal force`

@export By what day must the Court decide my appeal against a Federal Patent Court decision on a licence (Art 107(4))?
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act?
