GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court to decide my licence appeal` IS
    `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` `the appeal is against a decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act` `the day the appeal was brought`


§ `Simplified procedure (Art 108 and 109)`

@export May the president of the division alone decide not to enter on my appeal (Art 108(1))?
GIVEN `the appeal is obviously inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal obviously inadmissible?
      `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appeal obviously contain no sufficient reasoning?
      `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal querulous or an abuse of rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 108(1) the president of the division alone decides not to enter on my appeal` IS
    `Art 108(1) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry` `the appeal is obviously inadmissible` `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)` `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights`

@export Will the reasons I get be only a short statement of the ground of inadmissibility (Art 108(3))?
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of those that Art 108(1) gives to the president of the division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 108(3) the reasons I will get are a short statement of the ground` IS
    `Art 108(3) the reasons of the decision are confined to a short statement of the ground of inadmissibility` `the decision is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division`

-- Reading the answer: JUST TRUE means yes, the condition on which this kind of appeal is admissible (Art 74 and 83 to 85) is absent, so a bench of three may decide not to enter.
-- NOTHING means chapter 4 does not say: the condition is present, or the kind of appeal does not turn on such a condition.  This question never answers JUST FALSE.
-- Derived from chapter 3: Art 74(1) and (2) (a civil appeal below the value limit), Art 84(1), Art 84a and Art 85(1).  Not asked: the conditions of Art 83 (f)(1), (m), (w), (x), (z) and (zbis); for an appeal that turns on one of them the answer is NOTHING (fork F26).
@export May a bench of three judges decide not to enter on my appeal because the condition on which my kind of appeal is admissible, a question of fundamental importance or a particularly important case as Art 74 and 83 to 85 set it for this kind of appeal, is absent (Art 109(1))?
GIVEN `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters?
      `the subject of the legal assistance decision` IS A `Subject of a legal assistance decision` @desc What does the legal assistance decision concern: extradition, seizure, handing over of objects or assets, transmission of information from the secret sphere, or something else?
      `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated?
      `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects?
      `the case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case particularly important for reasons other than procedural violations or serious defects abroad?
      `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters?
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal raise a legal question of fundamental importance?
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one of money or property (a pecuniary matter)?
      `the decision is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of state liability?
      `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of public-law employment?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in francs?
      `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment law case?
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a tenancy law case?
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a federal statute provide for a single cantonal instance for your case (so that no second cantonal court decides)?
      `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter?
      `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of the bankruptcy and composition judge?
      `the body that decided` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision: the last cantonal instance, the Federal Administrative Court, the Federal Patent Court, a chamber of the Federal Criminal Court, the independent complaints authority for radio and television, or another body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 109(1) a bench of three judges decides not to enter on my appeal` IS
    `Art 109(1) with chapter 3 the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry` `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the subject of the legal assistance decision` `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` `the case is particularly important for other reasons` `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` `the value in dispute in francs` `the kind of appeal` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` `the body that decided`

@export May a bench of three judges decide my appeal if they are unanimous that it is obviously unfounded or obviously well founded (Art 109(2))?
GIVEN `the judges are unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the judges unanimous?
      `the appeal is obviously unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal obviously unfounded?
      `the appeal is obviously well founded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal obviously well founded?
      `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the challenged act depart from the Federal Supreme Court's case law, with no reason to review that case law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 109(2) a bench of three judges decides my appeal when they are unanimous` IS
    `Art 109(2) the division decides in a bench of three` `the judges are unanimous` `the appeal is obviously unfounded` `the appeal is obviously well founded` `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law`

@export Will the reasons of the bench of three be only summary (Art 109(3))?
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of those that Art 109(1) or (2) gives to a bench of three judges?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 109(3) the reasons I get are summary` IS
    `Art 109(3) the decision is given summary reasons` `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three`

@export May the reasons of the bench of three refer wholly or partly to the decision I challenged (Art 109(3), second sentence)?
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of those that Art 109(1) or (2) gives to a bench of three judges?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 109(3) the reasons I get may refer to the decision I challenged` IS
    `Art 109(3) the reasons may refer wholly or in part to the challenged decision` `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three`


§ `What the cantons must provide (Art 110 to 112)`

@export Has my canton ensured that a court freely reviewed the facts and applied the law of its own motion (Art 110, with Art 75(2), 80(2) and 86)?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `the decision is of predominantly political character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision of predominantly political character?
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a court, or a judicial authority that was competent earlier, freely review the facts?
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that court or authority apply the governing law of its own motion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 110 my canton has ensured the review by a court` IS
    `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `the kind of appeal` `the decision is of predominantly political character` `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts` `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion`

@export Must I be able to take part as a party before all the cantonal lower instances (Art 111(1), with Art 76(1), 81(1) and 89(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part, were you denied the chance to?
      `I am especially affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision affect you in a way that sets you apart from everyone else (are you especially affected)?
      `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest worthy of protection in having the decision quashed or changed?
      `my position in the criminal proceedings` IS A `Person in a criminal appeal` @desc What is your position in the criminal proceedings: the accused person, the accused person's legal representative, the public prosecutor's office, a private claimant, the person who filed the criminal complaint, the federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved in an administrative criminal matter, or another person?
      `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter: is the decision about ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention?
      `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you are a private claimant: can the decision affect how your civil claims are assessed?
      `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you filed the criminal complaint: does the appeal concern the right to file a criminal complaint as such?
      `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you are not named in the list: do you have a legally protected interest in having the decision quashed or changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 111(1) I must be able to take part as a party before all the cantonal lower instances` IS
    `Art 111(1) with chapter 3 the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` `the kind of appeal` `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` `I am especially affected by the decision` `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` `my position in the criminal proceedings` `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change`

@export Can the court directly below the Federal Supreme Court examine at least my complaints under Art 95 to 98 (Art 111(3))?
