      `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision contain a notice of the legal remedies available?
      `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act provide a value limit for this appeal?
      `the notice states the value in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the value in dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 112(1) my decision meets the requirements for a notified decision` IS
    `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision was notified to the parties in writing` `the decision contains the claims, the reasoning, the evidence offered and the procedural declarations of the parties` `those matters appear from the files` `the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and of law, in particular the statutory provisions applied` `the decision contains the operative part` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal` `the notice states the value in dispute`

@export Does my decision contain a notice of legal remedies, including the value in dispute where the Act gives a value limit (Art 112(1)(d), with Art 74(1) and 85(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Which kind of appeal is it: in civil matters, in criminal matters, in public-law matters, or another kind?
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one of money or property (a pecuniary matter)?
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment law case?
