      `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one that can be appealed to the Federal Supreme Court?
      `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision contain a notice of the legal remedies available?
      `the notice states the value in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the value in dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 112(1)(d) my decision has the notice of remedies with the value in dispute where required` IS
    `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `the kind of appeal` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` `the notice states the value in dispute`

@export May the authority notify my decision promptly and without reasons (Art 112(2), first sentence)?
