§ `Chapter 3 and chapter 4 together: may I appeal this decision at all, and by when?`

@export In a civil matter: may I appeal my decision, am I entitled to, can that act be appealed, is my appeal in time, and what is the time limit (Art 72, 76, 90 to 94, 100 and 101)?
GIVEN `the decision is in a civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in a civil matter?
      `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter?
      `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a public-law decision?
      `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a public-law decision: does it stand in immediate connection with civil law?
      `the kind of public-law decision` IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)` @desc If the decision is a public-law decision, which kind: recognition and enforcement of judgments or legal assistance in civil matters, keeping a register, a name change, supervision of foundations, supervision of executors, child and adult protection, or another kind?
      `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the decision concerns the supervision of a foundation: is the foundation a pension or vested-benefits institution?
      `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part, were you denied the chance to?
      `I am especially affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision affect you in a way that sets you apart from everyone else (are you especially affected)?
      `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest worthy of protection in having the decision quashed or changed?
      `what the appeal is brought against` IS A `Act challenged by the appeal` @desc What do you want to appeal against: a decision, a cantonal enactment, or an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision?
      `the decision ends the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the whole case in the court or authority that made it?
      `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision deal with only some of the claims made in the case?
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can those claims be judged independently of the claims the decision leaves open?
      `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the case for only some of the people who sued or were sued together?
      `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a preliminary or interim step, made before the final decision?
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision sent to you on its own, separately from the final decision?
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision rule on whether the court has jurisdiction, or on a request that a judge step aside?
      `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about international legal assistance in a criminal matter?
      `the matter is in the field of asylum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about asylum?
      `the decision is on extradition detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern detention pending extradition?
      `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern the seizure of assets or valuables?
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the decision cause you harm that could not be put right later?
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would upholding the appeal bring about a final decision straight away?
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that spare a significant amount of time or cost that a long evidence procedure would otherwise take?
      `the authority refused or delayed a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authority refuse to decide, or delay deciding?
      `the refusal or delay is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the refusal or delay unlawful?
      `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision that was refused or delayed one that could be appealed?
      `the kind of decision for the time limit` IS A `Kind of decision in Art 100(2) to (4)` @desc Which kind of decision is it for the time limit: a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy, in international legal assistance in criminal matters or administrative assistance in tax matters, on the return of a child, of the Federal Patent Court on a licence, of a cantonal government on a federal vote, of a cantonal government on a National Council election, or none of these?
      `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement?
      `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the complete version of the decision notified to you?
      `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal about a conflict of competence between two cantons?
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the first canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the second canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` IS A DATE @desc If you appeal against a cantonal enactment: on what day was it published, as cantonal law decides? (Any date otherwise.)
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the rules on suspension or restoration of time limits leave out of the count? (0 if none.)
      `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file, or will you file, the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court?
GIVETH A `Answers on appealing a decision and by when`
DECIDE `Art 72, 76 and 90 to 101 my civil decision: may I appeal, and by when` IS
    `Art 72, 76 and 90 to 101 the answers on appealing a civil decision and by when` `the decision is in a civil matter` `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` `the decision is a public-law decision` `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` `the kind of public-law decision` `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` `I am especially affected by the decision` `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` `what the appeal is brought against` `the decision ends the proceedings` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others` `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the matter is in the field of asylum` `the decision is on extradition detention` `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` `the authority refused or delayed a decision` `the refusal or delay is unlawful` `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` `the kind of decision for the time limit` `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court`

@export In a criminal matter: may I appeal my decision, am I entitled to, can that act be appealed, is my appeal in time, and what is the time limit (Art 78, 81, 90 to 94, 100 and 101)?
GIVEN `the decision is in a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in a criminal matter?
      `the decision is on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter: is the decision on civil claims?
      `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the civil claims to be dealt with together with the criminal matter?
      `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision on the execution of penalties and measures?
      `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part, were you denied the chance to?
      `my position in the criminal proceedings` IS A `Person in a criminal appeal` @desc What is your position in the criminal proceedings: the accused person, the accused person's legal representative, the public prosecutor's office, a private claimant, the person who filed the criminal complaint, the federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved in an administrative criminal matter, or another person?
      `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter: is the decision about ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention?
      `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you are a private claimant: can the decision affect how your civil claims are assessed?
      `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you filed the criminal complaint: does the appeal concern the right to file a criminal complaint as such?
      `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a criminal matter, if you are not named in the list: do you have a legally protected interest in having the decision quashed or changed?
      `what the appeal is brought against` IS A `Act challenged by the appeal` @desc What do you want to appeal against: a decision, a cantonal enactment, or an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision?
      `the decision ends the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the whole case in the court or authority that made it?
      `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision deal with only some of the claims made in the case?
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can those claims be judged independently of the claims the decision leaves open?
      `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision end the case for only some of the people who sued or were sued together?
      `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a preliminary or interim step, made before the final decision?
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision sent to you on its own, separately from the final decision?
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision rule on whether the court has jurisdiction, or on a request that a judge step aside?
      `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about international legal assistance in a criminal matter?
      `the matter is in the field of asylum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter about asylum?
      `the decision is on extradition detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern detention pending extradition?
      `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision concern the seizure of assets or valuables?
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the decision cause you harm that could not be put right later?
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would upholding the appeal bring about a final decision straight away?
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that spare a significant amount of time or cost that a long evidence procedure would otherwise take?
      `the authority refused or delayed a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authority refuse to decide, or delay deciding?
      `the refusal or delay is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the refusal or delay unlawful?
      `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision that was refused or delayed one that could be appealed?
      `the kind of decision for the time limit` IS A `Kind of decision in Art 100(2) to (4)` @desc Which kind of decision is it for the time limit: a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy, in international legal assistance in criminal matters or administrative assistance in tax matters, on the return of a child, of the Federal Patent Court on a licence, of a cantonal government on a federal vote, of a cantonal government on a National Council election, or none of these?
      `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement?
      `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the complete version of the decision notified to you?
      `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal about a conflict of competence between two cantons?
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the first canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` IS A DATE @desc In an intercantonal conflict: on what day was a decision that can be appealed taken in the second canton? (Any date if it is not such a conflict.)
      `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` IS A DATE @desc If you appeal against a cantonal enactment: on what day was it published, as cantonal law decides? (Any date otherwise.)
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the rules on suspension or restoration of time limits leave out of the count? (0 if none.)
      `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file, or will you file, the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court?
GIVETH A `Answers on appealing a decision and by when`
DECIDE `Art 78, 81 and 90 to 101 my criminal decision: may I appeal, and by when` IS
    `Art 78, 81 and 90 to 101 the answers on appealing a criminal decision and by when` `the decision is in a criminal matter` `the decision is on civil claims` `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` `my position in the criminal proceedings` `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` `what the appeal is brought against` `the decision ends the proceedings` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others` `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the matter is in the field of asylum` `the decision is on extradition detention` `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` `the authority refused or delayed a decision` `the refusal or delay is unlawful` `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` `the kind of decision for the time limit` `the decision is made in the course of bill-of-exchange enforcement` `the day the complete version of the decision was notified` `the appeal concerns an intercantonal conflict of competence` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the first canton` `the day a decision that can be appealed was taken in the second canton` `the day of the publication that is decisive under cantonal law` `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` `the day the appeal was filed with the Federal Supreme Court`

